#: ../../../gpu/building.rst:131
msgid "Build overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/building.rst:133
msgid ""
"Once installed, the GPU build will create several files used for different "
"targets. This section will briefly describe their purpose."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/building.rst:136
msgid "**include/<target-triple>**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/building.rst:137
msgid ""
"The include directory where all of the generated headers for the target will "
"go. These definitions are strictly for the GPU when being targeted directly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/building.rst:140
msgid ""
"**lib/clang/<llvm-major-version>/include/llvm-libc-wrappers/llvm-libc-decls**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/building.rst:141
msgid ""
"These are wrapper headers created for offloading languages like CUDA, HIP, "
"or OpenMP. They contain functions supported in the GPU libc along with "
"attributes and metadata that declare them on the target device and make them "
"compatible with the host headers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/building.rst:146
msgid "**lib/<target-triple>/libc.a**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/building.rst:147
msgid ""
"The main C library static archive containing LLVM-IR targeting the given "
"GPU. It can be linked directly or inspected depending on the target support."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/building.rst:150
msgid "**lib/<target-triple>/libm.a**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/building.rst:151
msgid ""
"The C library static archive providing implementations of the standard math "
"functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/building.rst:154
msgid "**lib/<target-triple>/libc.bc**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/building.rst:155
msgid ""
"An alternate form of the library provided as a single LLVM-IR bitcode blob. "
"This can be used similarly to NVIDIA's or AMD's device libraries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/building.rst:158
msgid "**lib/<target-triple>/libm.bc**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/building.rst:159
msgid ""
"An alternate form of the library provided as a single LLVM-IR bitcode blob "
"containing the standard math functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/building.rst:162
msgid "**lib/<target-triple>/crt1.o**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/building.rst:163
msgid ""
"An LLVM-IR file containing startup code to call the ``main`` function on the "
"GPU. This is used similarly to the standard C library startup object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/building.rst:166
msgid "**bin/amdhsa-loader**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/building.rst:167
msgid ""
"A binary utility used to launch executables compiled targeting the AMD GPU. "
"This will be included if the build system found the ``hsa-runtime64`` "
"library either in ``/opt/rocm`` or the current CMake installation directory. "
"This is required to build the GPU tests .See the :ref:`libc GPU "
"usage<libc_gpu_usage>` for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/building.rst:173
msgid "**bin/nvptx-loader**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/building.rst:174
msgid ""
"A binary utility used to launch executables compiled targeting the NVIDIA "
"GPU. This will be included if the build system found the CUDA driver API. "
"This is required for building tests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/building.rst:178
msgid "**include/llvm-libc-rpc-server.h**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/building.rst:179
msgid ""
"A header file containing definitions that can be used to interface with the :"
"ref:`RPC server<libc_gpu_rpc>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/building.rst:182
msgid "**lib/libllvmlibc_rpc_server.a**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/building.rst:183
msgid ""
"The static library containing the implementation of the RPC server. This can "
"be used to enable host services for anyone looking to interface with the :"
"ref:`RPC client<libc_gpu_rpc>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/building.rst:190
msgid "CMake options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/building.rst:192
msgid ""
"This section briefly lists a few of the CMake variables that specifically "
"control the GPU build of the C library. These options can be passed "
"individually to each target using ``-DRUNTIMES_<target>_<variable>=<value>`` "
"when using a standard runtime build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/building.rst:197
msgid "**LLVM_LIBC_FULL_BUILD**:BOOL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/building.rst:198
msgid ""
"This flag controls whether or not the libc build will generate its own "
"headers. This must always be on when targeting the GPU."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/building.rst:201
msgid "**LIBC_GPU_BUILD**:BOOL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/building.rst:202
msgid ""
"Shorthand for enabling GPU support. Equivalent to enabling support for both "
"AMDGPU and NVPTX builds for ``libc``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/building.rst:205
msgid "**LIBC_GPU_TEST_ARCHITECTURE**:STRING"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/building.rst:206
msgid ""
"Sets the architecture used to build the GPU tests for, such as ``gfx90a`` or "
"``sm_80`` for AMD and NVIDIA GPUs respectively. The default behavior is to "
"detect the system's GPU architecture using the ``native`` option. If this "
"option is not set and a GPU was not detected the tests will not be built."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/building.rst:211
msgid "**LIBC_GPU_TEST_JOBS**:STRING"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/building.rst:212
msgid ""
"Sets the number of threads used to run GPU tests. The GPU test suite will "
"commonly run out of resources if this is not constrained so it is "
"recommended to keep it low. The default value is a single thread."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/building.rst:216
msgid "**CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING_EMULATOR**:STRING"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/building.rst:217
msgid ""
"Overrides the default loader used for running GPU tests. This is set "
"automatically to ``llvm-gpu-loader`` for GPU runtime targets when building "
"via the runtimes build."
msgstr ""
